/-!
# The special fibre of a model is a principal divisor

Let `X ⟶ Spec(R)` be flat over a discrete valuation ring `R` with uniformizer `π`. The special
fibre `X_k` is the closed subscheme of `X` cut out by the image of `π`, and it is an effective
Cartier divisor. Its sheaf of ideals is generated by the *single global* function coming from
`π`, so `X_k` is the zero scheme of a regular global section of the structure sheaf; the
correspondence between effective Cartier divisors and invertible modules with a regular section
then trivializes the associated invertible sheaf, `𝒪_X(X_k) ≅ 𝒪_X`.

## Main definitions

* `Stacks.Models.RegularModelSituation.specialFiberIdeal` — the special fibre of a regular model
  as a quasi-coherent sheaf of ideals on the total space.
* `Stacks.Models.chartHom` — the ring map `R ⟶ Γ(X, U)` through which a scheme over `R` makes
  the functions on an open an `R`-algebra.
* `Stacks.Models.uniformizerSection` — an element of the base ring, read as a global section of
  the structure sheaf regarded as a module over itself.

## Main results

* `Stacks.Models.isEffectiveCartierDivisor_specialFiberIdeal` — the special fibre of a regular
  model is an effective Cartier divisor.
* `Stacks.Models.specialFiberIdeal_ideal_eq_span` — on every affine open the ideal of the
  special fibre is generated by the image of the uniformizer.
* `Stacks.Models.zeroScheme_uniformizerSection_eq_ker` and
  `Stacks.Models.zeroScheme_uniformizer_eq_specialFiberIdeal` — the special fibre is the zero
  scheme of the uniformizer, read as a global section of the structure sheaf.
* `Stacks.Models.isRegularSection_uniformizerSection` — that global section is regular.
* `Stacks.Models.invertibleSheafIsoUnit_specialFiber` and
  `Stacks.Models.invertibleSheafIso_specialFiberIdeal` — the invertible sheaf of the special
  fibre is trivial, `𝒪_X(X_k) ≅ 𝒪_X`, for a flat scheme over a discrete valuation ring and
  hence for a regular proper model.

## Implementation notes

`Stacks.Models.RegularModelSituation.specialFiber` is the fibre product `X ×_{Spec R} Spec(k)`
*as a scheme*; `Stacks.Models.RegularModelSituation.specialFiberIdeal` is a different object,
the sheaf of ideals cutting that fibre out as a closed subscheme of `X`. The Cartier
theorem `Stacks.Models.isEffectiveCartierDivisor_specialFiber` is about the latter, and is
restated here at the level of the situation.

Regularity of the global section is obtained from the Cartier theorem through
`AlgebraicGeometry.isEffectiveCartierDivisor_zeroScheme_iff_isRegularSection`, rather than from
`Stacks.Models.map_mem_nonZeroDivisors_of_flat` directly: the identification of the special
fibre with the zero scheme of the uniformizer is needed in any case, and once it is available
the Cartier property transports to regularity with no second local computation and no further
retyping between `nonZeroDivisors`, `IsRegular` and `IsSMulRegular`.

The invertible sheaf of a divisor is taken in the primed family of
`StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.Divisors.DivisorInvertibleSheaf`, which is the one the rest of
the divisor API speaks. Invertibility of the structure sheaf as a module over itself is
available in the library only at other, definitionally equal, spellings of the sheaf of rings;
since instance search is syntactic it is rebound here with a declared type at the spelling
`(X.sheaf.obj, X.ringCatSheaf.property)` that the zero-scheme API uses.

## References

* [Stacks Project, Tag 0C5Z](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0C5Z)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 01X0](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/01X0)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 02OR](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/02OR)
-/

@[expose] public section

open AlgebraicGeometry CategoryTheory Limits Opposite
open Stacks.Divisors

namespace Stacks.Models

universe u

/-! ### The special fibre as a sheaf of ideals -/

namespace RegularModelSituation

/-- The special fibre `X_k` of a regular model as a quasi-coherent sheaf of ideals on the total
space: the kernel of the first projection of `X ×_{Spec R} Spec(k)`. This is the ideal cutting
out the closed subscheme, not the fibre product itself. -/
public noncomputable abbrev specialFiberIdeal (S : RegularModelSituation.{u}) :
    S.X.IdealSheafData :=
  (pullback.fst S.X_to_R (Spec.map (CommRingCat.ofHom (algebraMap S.R S.k)))).ker

end RegularModelSituation

/-- The special fibre of a regular model is an effective Cartier divisor on the total space:
flatness over the discrete valuation ring makes a uniformizer a nonzerodivisor on every affine
chart, and the special fibre is its zero scheme there. -/
@[sga "6 X 7.2" "special case"]
public instance isEffectiveCartierDivisor_specialFiberIdeal (S : RegularModelSituation.{u}) :
    IsEffectiveCartierDivisor S.specialFiberIdeal :=
  isEffectiveCartierDivisor_specialFiber S.residueEquiv S.X_to_R

/-- The structure sheaf of a scheme, viewed as a module over itself, is invertible: it is the
unit of the tensor product of sheaves of modules. -/
public instance isInvertible_unit (X : Scheme.{u}) :
    AlgebraicGeometry.SheafOfModules.IsInvertible X.sheaf.obj X.ringCatSheaf.property
      (SheafOfModules.unit X.ringCatSheaf) :=
  Stacks.SheafOfModules.IsInvertible.toAlgebraicGeometry _ _ _
    (Stacks.SheafOfModules.isInvertible_unit X.sheaf.obj X.ringCatSheaf.property)

/-! ### Functions coming from the base ring -/

section Chart

variable {R : Type u} [CommRing R] {X : Scheme.{u}}

/-- The ring map `R ⟶ Γ(X, U)` through which a scheme over `R` makes the functions on an open
`U ⊆ X` an `R`-algebra: the pullback of global functions on `Spec(R)`, restricted to `U`. -/
public noncomputable def chartHom (f : X ⟶ Spec (.of R)) (U : X.Opens) :
    CommRingCat.of R ⟶ Γ(X, U) :=
  (Scheme.ΓSpecIso (CommRingCat.of R)).inv ≫ f.appLE ⊤ U (by simp)

/-- The functions coming from the base ring are compatible with restriction: the function cut
out on a smaller open is the restriction of the one cut out on a larger one. -/
public theorem chartHom_comp_map (f : X ⟶ Spec (.of R)) {V W : (X.Opens)ᵒᵖ} (i : V ⟶ W) :
    chartHom f V.unop ≫ X.presheaf.map i = chartHom f W.unop := by
  dsimp only [chartHom]
  rw [Category.assoc, Scheme.Hom.appLE_map]

/-- An element of the base ring, read as a global section of the structure sheaf of a scheme
over that ring regarded as a module over itself: its component on an open is the function the
element cuts out there. -/
public noncomputable def uniformizerSection (f : X ⟶ Spec (.of R)) (r : R) :
    (SheafOfModules.unit X.ringCatSheaf).sections :=
  PresheafOfModules.sectionsMk (fun V ↦ show Γ(X, V.unop) from (chartHom f V.unop).hom r)
    (fun {V W} i ↦ by
      change X.presheaf.map i ((chartHom f V.unop).hom r) = (chartHom f W.unop).hom r
      exact congrArg (fun ψ : CommRingCat.of R ⟶ Γ(X, W.unop) ↦ ψ.hom r)
        (chartHom_comp_map f i))

/-- The component on the whole space of the global section of the structure sheaf determined by
an element of the base ring is the global function that element cuts out. -/
public theorem uniformizerSection_eval_top (f : X ⟶ Spec (.of R)) (r : R) :
    (uniformizerSection f r).eval (op ⊤) = (chartHom f (⊤ : X.Opens)).hom r := rfl

end Chart

/-! ### The special fibre is the zero scheme of the uniformizer -/

section Model

variable {R k : Type u} [CommRing R] [IsDomain R] [IsDiscreteValuationRing R]
  [Field k] [Algebra R k] {X : Scheme.{u}}

/-- **The local equation of the special fibre.** On every affine open `U ⊆ X` the ideal of the
special fibre of a scheme flat over a discrete valuation ring is the principal ideal generated
by the function a uniformizer cuts out on `U`. -/
@[sga "6 X 7.8" "partial"]
public theorem specialFiberIdeal_ideal_eq_span
    (residueEquiv : IsLocalRing.ResidueField R ≃ₐ[R] k)
    (f : X ⟶ Spec (.of R)) [Flat f] {π : R} (hπ : Irreducible π)
    (U : X.Opens) (hU : IsAffineOpen U) :
    (pullback.fst f (Spec.map (CommRingCat.ofHom (algebraMap R k)))).ker.ideal ⟨U, hU⟩ =
      Ideal.span {(chartHom f U).hom π} := by
  let g : Spec (.of k) ⟶ Spec (.of R) := Spec.map (CommRingCat.ofHom (algebraMap R k))
  let I : X.IdealSheafData := (pullback.fst f g).ker
  let φ := chartHom f U
  let _ : Algebra R Γ(X, U) := φ.hom.toAlgebra
  have hj : hU.fromSpec ≫ f = Spec.map (CommRingCat.ofHom (algebraMap R Γ(X, U))) := by
    change hU.fromSpec ≫ f = Spec.map φ
    dsimp [φ, chartHom]
    rw [Spec.map_comp]
    simpa [Scheme.isoSpec_Spec_inv, IsAffineOpen.fromSpec_top] using
      (IsAffineOpen.SpecMap_appLE_fromSpec f (isAffineOpen_top (Spec (.of R))) hU (by simp)).symm
  let J := Ideal.span ({π} : Set R)
  let E : (R ⧸ J) ≃ₐ[R] k :=
    (Ideal.quotientEquivAlgOfEq R hπ.maximalIdeal_eq.symm).trans residueEquiv
  let q : Spec (.of (R ⧸ J)) ⟶ Spec (.of R) :=
    Spec.map (CommRingCat.ofHom (Ideal.Quotient.mk J))
  let eSpec : Spec (.of k) ≅ Spec (.of (R ⧸ J)) :=
    Scheme.Spec.mapIso E.toRingEquiv.toCommRingCatIso.op
  have hg : g = eSpec.hom ≫ q := by
    have hmap : algebraMap R k = E.toAlgHom.toRingHom.comp (Ideal.Quotient.mk J) := by
      ext r
      exact (E.commutes r).symm
    change Spec.map (CommRingCat.ofHom (algebraMap R k)) = _
    rw [show eSpec.hom = Spec.map (CommRingCat.ofHom E.toAlgHom.toRingHom) by
      simp [eSpec, Functor.mapIso_hom, Iso.op_hom, Scheme.Spec_map], ← Spec.map_comp,
      ← CommRingCat.ofHom_comp]
    exact congrArg (fun ψ ↦ Spec.map (CommRingCat.ofHom ψ)) hmap
  have : IsClosedImmersion q :=
    IsClosedImmersion.spec_of_surjective _ Ideal.Quotient.mk_surjective
  have : IsClosedImmersion g := by
    rw [hg]
    infer_instance
  let pIso : pullback f g ≅ I.subscheme := asIso (pullback.fst f g).toImage
  let pbMap := pullback.map f g f q (𝟙 X) eSpec.hom (𝟙 (Spec (.of R))) (by simp) hg
  have : IsIso pbMap :=
    pullback.map_isIso f g f q (𝟙 X) eSpec.hom (𝟙 (Spec (.of R))) (by simp) hg
  let fibreIso : I.subscheme ≅ pullback f q := pIso.symm ≪≫ asIso pbMap
  have hfibre : fibreIso.hom ≫ pullback.fst f q = I.subschemeι := by
    have hpmap : pbMap ≫ pullback.fst f q = pullback.fst f g := by
      dsimp [pbMap, pullback.map]
      rw [pullback.lift_fst]
      simp
    change pIso.symm.hom ≫ pbMap ≫ pullback.fst f q = I.subschemeι
    rw [hpmap, ← Scheme.Hom.toImage_imageι (f := pullback.fst f g)]
    simp [pIso, I]
  let fibreChart : pullback I.subschemeι U.ι ≅ pullback (hU.fromSpec ≫ f) q := by
    let i₁ := pullback.map I.subschemeι U.ι (pullback.fst f q) U.ι fibreIso.hom
      (𝟙 U.toScheme) (𝟙 X) (by simpa using hfibre.symm) (by simp)
    have : IsIso i₁ := pullback.map_isIso I.subschemeι U.ι (pullback.fst f q) U.ι
      fibreIso.hom (𝟙 U.toScheme) (𝟙 X) hfibre.symm (by simp)
    let i₂ := pullback.map (U.ι ≫ f) q (hU.fromSpec ≫ f) q hU.isoSpec.hom
      (𝟙 (Spec (.of (R ⧸ J)))) (𝟙 (Spec (.of R))) (by simp) (by simp)
    exact asIso i₁ ≪≫ pullbackSymmetry (pullback.fst f q) U.ι ≪≫
      pullbackRightPullbackFstIso f q U.ι ≪≫ asIso i₂
  have hchart : fibreChart.hom ≫ pullback.fst (hU.fromSpec ≫ f) q =
      pullback.snd I.subschemeι U.ι ≫ hU.isoSpec.hom := by
    simp only [fibreChart, Iso.trans_hom, asIso_hom, Category.assoc, pullback.map]
    simp only [← Category.assoc, pullback.lift_fst, pullback.lift_snd,
      pullbackSymmetry_hom_comp_fst, pullbackRightPullbackFstIso_hom_fst, Category.comp_id]
  change _ = Ideal.span {algebraMap R Γ(X, U) π}
  refine ideal_eq_quotient_of_chart I U hU (Ideal.span {algebraMap R Γ(X, U) π})
    (fibreChart ≪≫ specialFiberAffineOpenIso π f hU.fromSpec hj) ?_
  simpa [q, J, Category.assoc, specialFiberAffineOpenIso_hom_fst π f hU.fromSpec hj] using
    hchart.symm

/-- **The special fibre is the zero scheme of a uniformizer.** The sheaf of ideals of the
special fibre of a scheme flat over a discrete valuation ring is cut out by the single global
function a uniformizer determines. -/
@[sga "6 X 7.8" "partial"]
public theorem zeroScheme_uniformizerSection_eq_ker
    (residueEquiv : IsLocalRing.ResidueField R ≃ₐ[R] k)
    (f : X ⟶ Spec (.of R)) [Flat f] {π : R} (hπ : Irreducible π) :
    AlgebraicGeometry.zeroScheme X (SheafOfModules.unit X.ringCatSheaf)
        ((uniformizerSection f π).eval (op ⊤)) =
      (pullback.fst f (Spec.map (CommRingCat.ofHom (algebraMap R k)))).ker := by
  let L : X.Modules := SheafOfModules.unit X.ringCatSheaf
  refine Scheme.IdealSheafData.ext ?_
  funext V
  obtain ⟨V, hV⟩ := V
  rw [specialFiberIdeal_ideal_eq_span (k := k) residueEquiv f hπ V hV]
  refine AlgebraicGeometry.zeroScheme_ideal_of_trivialization X L
    ((uniformizerSection f π).eval (op ⊤)) ⟨V, hV⟩ (LinearEquiv.refl _ _) ((chartHom f V).hom π) ?_
  exact congrArg (fun ψ : CommRingCat.of R ⟶ Γ(X, V) ↦ ψ.hom π)
    (chartHom_comp_map f (homOfLE (le_top : V ≤ ⊤)).op)

/-- **The uniformizer is a regular global section.** Its zero scheme is the special fibre, an
effective Cartier divisor, and the zero scheme of a global section of an invertible module is an
effective Cartier divisor exactly when the section is a nonzerodivisor. -/
@[sga "6 X 7.2" "(g)"]
public theorem isRegularSection_uniformizerSection
    (residueEquiv : IsLocalRing.ResidueField R ≃ₐ[R] k)
    (f : X ⟶ Spec (.of R)) [Flat f] {π : R} (hπ : Irreducible π) :
    IsRegularSection X.sheaf.obj X.ringCatSheaf.property (uniformizerSection f π) := by
  refine (isEffectiveCartierDivisor_zeroScheme_iff_isRegularSection X
    (SheafOfModules.unit X.ringCatSheaf) (uniformizerSection f π)).mp ?_
  rw [zeroScheme_uniformizerSection_eq_ker (k := k) residueEquiv f hπ]
  exact isEffectiveCartierDivisor_specialFiber residueEquiv f

/-- **The invertible sheaf of the special fibre is trivial**, `𝒪_X(X_k) ≅ 𝒪_X`, for any scheme
flat over a discrete valuation ring: the special fibre is the zero scheme of the regular global
section determined by a uniformizer, and the divisor of a regular section of an invertible
module reproduces that module. -/
@[stacks 0C5Z "part (4): the special fibre has trivial invertible sheaf",
  sga "6 X 7.8" "O_X(X_s) ≅ O_X"]
public noncomputable def invertibleSheafIsoUnit_specialFiber
    (residueEquiv : IsLocalRing.ResidueField R ≃ₐ[R] k)
    (f : X ⟶ Spec (.of R)) [Flat f] {π : R} (hπ : Irreducible π) :
    invertibleSheaf' (pullback.fst f (Spec.map (CommRingCat.ofHom (algebraMap R k)))).ker ≅
      SheafOfModules.unit X.ringCatSheaf := by
  have h := existsUnique_invertibleSheafIso_zeroScheme X (SheafOfModules.unit X.ringCatSheaf)
    (uniformizerSection f π) (isRegularSection_uniformizerSection (k := k) residueEquiv f hπ)
  rw [zeroScheme_uniformizerSection_eq_ker (k := k) residueEquiv f hπ] at h
  exact h.exists.choose

end Model

/-! ### Triviality of the invertible sheaf of the special fibre -/

/-- **The special fibre of a regular proper model is the zero scheme of its uniformizer**, read
as a global section of the structure sheaf regarded as a module over itself. -/
public theorem zeroScheme_uniformizer_eq_specialFiberIdeal
    (S : RegularProperModelSituation.{u}) :
    AlgebraicGeometry.zeroScheme S.X (SheafOfModules.unit S.X.ringCatSheaf)
        ((uniformizerSection S.X_to_R S.π).eval (op ⊤)) = S.specialFiberIdeal :=
  zeroScheme_uniformizerSection_eq_ker (k := S.k) S.residueEquiv S.X_to_R S.uniformizer

/-- **Stacks Project, Tag 0C5Z (4).** The invertible sheaf of the special fibre of a regular
proper model is trivial, `𝒪_X(X_k) ≅ 𝒪_X`: the special fibre is the zero scheme of the regular
global section determined by a uniformizer, and the divisor of a regular section of an
invertible module reproduces that module. -/
public noncomputable def invertibleSheafIso_specialFiberIdeal
    (S : RegularProperModelSituation.{u}) :
    invertibleSheaf' S.specialFiberIdeal ≅ SheafOfModules.unit S.X.ringCatSheaf :=
  invertibleSheafIsoUnit_specialFiber (k := S.k) S.residueEquiv S.X_to_R S.uniformizer

end Stacks.Models

end
